---
source: tests/steps/l01_06_lexer_tokens/words.rs
expression: "out.join(\"\\n\")"
---
# none       [0..1] `#` starts an atom, and the atom's name must follow it at once, as in `#none`. Write the name right after the `#`, with no space between.
x = @        [4..5] `@` starts an annotation, and the annotation's name must follow it at once, as in `@test`. Write the name right after the `@`, with no space between.
#pаypal      [0..8] `#pаypal` is no atom: `а` (U+0430) is not ASCII. Try `#paypal` instead.
cost = $5    [7..8] the character `$` (U+0024) starts no name, number, operator or other part of a Zed program. Remove it, or, if it is meant as text, write it inside a string, as `"$"`.
a % b        [2..3] the character `%` (U+0025) starts no name, number, operator or other part of a Zed program. Remove it, or, if it is meant as text, write it inside a string, as `"%"`.
x ~ y        [2..3] the character `~` (U+007E) starts no name, number, operator or other part of a Zed program. Remove it, or, if it is meant as text, write it inside a string, as `"~"`.
`cmd`        [0..1] the character `` ` `` (U+0060) starts no name, number, operator or other part of a Zed program. Remove it, or, if it is meant as text, write it inside a string, as `` "`" ``.
x''          [2..3] `'` stands only right after a name, once, as in `x'`, and starts nothing by itself. Remove this `'`, or write it right after the name it marks.
